        /// <summary>
        /// Promote release fix to Code System branch.
        /// </summary>
        /// <remarks>
        /// In an authoring terminology server; if small content changes have to be made to a code system version after it's been created the changes can be applied to the release branch and then merged back to the main code system branch using this function. This function performs the following steps: 1. The changes are merged to the parent branch at a point in time immediately after the latest version was created. 2. The version branch is rebased to this new commit. 3. A second commit is made at a point in time immediately after the fix commit to revert the changes. This is necessary to preserve the integrity of more recent commits on the code system branch made during the new ongoing authoring cycle. The fixes should be applied to head timepoint of the code system branch using an alternative method.
        /// </remarks>
        /// <returns>OK</returns>
        /// <exception cref="ApiException">A server side error occurred.</exception>
        System.Threading.Tasks.Task PromoteReleaseFixAsync(string releaseFixBranch);

